BIB                 11         34
TITLE      Systematic study of (p,n) and (p,2n) reactions on
            110Cd
AUTHOR     (V.Vashi, R.Makwana, B.Quintana, M.H.Mehta, R.K.Singh,
            B.K.Soni, R.Chauhan, S.Mukherjee, M.Abhangi, S.Vala,
            N.L.Singh, G.B.Patel, S.V.Suryanarayana, B.K.Nayak,
            S.C.Sharma, T.N.Nag, Y.Kavun)
INSTITUTE  (3INDBDA,3INDGND,3INDMNP,3INDTRM)
           (2SPNSPN) Universidad de Salamanca, Calle Espejo s/n,
            Salmanca
           (2TUKTUK) Kahramanmaras Sutcu Imam University,
            Kahramanmaras
           (3INDIND) Homi Bhabha National Institute,
             Anushaktinagar, Mumbai
REFERENCE  (J,RPC,208,110933,2023)
           #doi:10.1016/j.radphyschem.2023.110933
FACILITY   (VDGT,3INDTAT) BARC-TIFR Pelletron Facility
SAMPLE     (48-CD-110,NAT=0.1249) NatCd target of ~250 micron
            thickness followed by Cu degrader of ~ 3.56 um, and
            wrapped with Al foil.
DETECTOR   (HPGE) A pre-calibrated detector coupled to a
            multi-channel analyzer was used. The detector was
            calibrated using a 152Eu multi-gamma source.
METHOD     (ACTIV) The samples were irradiated at a constant
            current of 150 nA for a suitable duration and cooled
            for about eight hours before measurement.
STATUS     (APRVD) Approved by R. Makwana (2026-09-21)
           (TABLE,,V.Vashi+,J,RPC,208,110933,2023) Table 3
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-T) The total uncertainty was determined from the
            quadratic sum of the individual uncertainties.
           (ERR-S,,3.) Counting statistics (<=2-3%)
           (ERR-1,,3.) Efficiency of the detector (<=3%)
           (ERR-2,,0.001) Mass (<=0.001%)
           (ERR-3,,0.5) Decay parameters (<=0.5%)
HISTORY    (20260914C) Paresh Prajapati - AASPP Workshop,2026
